/-!
# Component analysis for escaping centralizers

The first assertion of E.6.8 and its common fixed-space and local residual
deductions are proved in `Basic`. `Models` specifies all five source alternatives
and the precise intrinsic torus actions needed by E.6.11, using actual group
isomorphisms and embedded subgroups.

The characteristic-two and remaining-component sieves and the Borel/parabolic
torus constructions are still required. This module does not yet export a
theorem asserting the alternatives or E.6.11. The E.6.8 assembly will keep the
permitted earlier Chapter 1 inputs and E.6.7 block input explicit until its
parent discharges them.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), E.6.8 and
E.6.11, printed pp.247–250 (PDF pp.258–261).
-/
